codex
Wrote the A2 report to [cartflows-agent-a2.json](/Volumes/External_Disk/timo/WORDPRESS-PLUGIN-RESEARCH/reports/cartflows-agent-a2.json). It validates against [agent-output.schema.json](/Volumes/External_Disk/timo/WORDPRESS-PLUGIN-RESEARCH/contracts/agent-output.schema.json).

Result set: 22 entry points reviewed, 1 TP, 21 FP. The confirmed issue is the shared checkout upload handler at [class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php:293](/Volumes/External_Disk/timo/WORDPRESS-PLUGIN-RESEARCH/plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php#L293), where the nonce is exposed on public checkout pages and uploads are accepted without requiring a real `field_key`/`checkout_id` context, allowing arbitrary public media uploads to `wp-content/uploads/`. I also noted the missing `reports/cartflows-threat-context.json` input and narrowed claims to the code that was actually present.
